Overall Summary of My Work Readiness Training

This digital portfolio represents my journey through the Work Readiness Training modules for the PRP370S Project Presentation 3 course. 
Each section contains evidence of my completed assessments and a detailed reflection on my learning experience, 
written using the STAR technique (Situation, Task, Action, Result).

Through these modules, I have developed a strong foundation in key professional skills:

   Business Communication: I learned how to write clear, professional emails and communicate effectively in virtual settings.
   Interview Skills: I mastered the CAR method for answering behavioral questions and learned how to present myself confidently in an interview.
   Mock Interview: I gained practical experience and received valuable feedback that helped me refine my approach to real job interviews.
   Professional Networking: I understood the importance of building genuine, reciprocal relationships and avoiding common networking mistakes.
   Workplace Etiquette: I learned the unwritten rules of professional conduct, including how to handle difficult situations and maintain confidentiality.

This training has not only improved my technical knowledge but also boosted my confidence and preparedness for entering the professional world. 
I am now equipped with the skills and mindset needed to succeed in a modern workplace.
